# Frontend (`apps/web`)

Next.js App Router, React, TanStack Form + Query, Better Auth **client** (`lib/auth` → Hono `/api/auth/*`), Tailwind CSS **v4**, shadcn/base-nova under `components/ui/`.

Placement: **`layering`** + **`structure`**.

## Naming

Feature/component files: `kebab-case` (`sign-in-form.tsx`); PascalCase exports. Routes: `page.tsx` / `layout.tsx`.

## TypeScript

- Extend `../../tsconfig.base.json`; Next options (`jsx`/`bundler`/`plugins`/`paths` `@/*`) local

## Layout

| Layer | Location | Pattern |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Routes | `app/**` | thin pages; compose features |
| Features | `features/**` | domain UI, forms, feature hooks |
| Design system | `components/ui/` | shadcn atoms only |
| Shared non-feature UI | `components/` | providers/shell |
| Auth client | `lib/auth/` | `better-auth/react` client; BA session cookie via `/api/auth/*` proxy |
| Server state | `lib/query/` | TanStack Query |
| Client UI state | `stores/` | Zustand UI-only (create when needed) |
| Validation | `lib/validations/` | form Zod; auth bounds from `@gloaming/shared/auth/policy` |
| Constants | `constants/` | literals used 2+ times |
| Assets | `public/` | optional (`.gitkeep` OK) |

- Prefer existing `components/ui/`; shadcn CLI; ask before editing `components/ui/**` source
- Zustand: UI-only — never API/server SoT (`layering`)

### Feature page composition (anti–god component)

Prefer **compose many focused components** over one 700–1000 line page module.

| Rule | Detail |
| --- | --- |
| Thin route | `app/**/page.tsx` only passes params / renders a feature entry |
| Page = orchestrator | `*-page.tsx` owns data load, empty/error gates, layout chrome; delegates UI surfaces |
| Colocate siblings | Page-owned pieces live next to the page under `features/<domain>/` (same dir), not in a catch-all `components/` |
| Size ceiling | Soft ~300–400 lines; hard split at **>500** — see `structure` Feature UI size ceiling |
| Isolation | Keep selection state, chat/rail state, form editor state in their owning child; parent passes props / callbacks |
| When to split vs wait | Split structure **before** wiring the next real API into a megacomponent — do not wait for “full real data” to carve boundaries |
| Not this rule | Stub/mock honesty, data-flow bugs, and `formatXApiError = formatApiError` aliases — fix those separately; splitting alone does not fix them |

Example shape:

```text
features/reader/
  reader-page.tsx          # session + chrome + compose
  reader-part.tsx          # current ReadingPart body + selection toolbar
  reader-ai-drawer.tsx     # assist drawer
```

Shared content helpers live in `features/content/content-model.ts` (cover tints, paragraph split). Domain: **ReadingWork** / **ReadingPart** — see ADR-001; do not add **ArticleLevel** or article-centric types in new feature code (Phase 3 migrates legacy).

## Styling

Tailwind v4 (`@import "tailwindcss"`); semantic tokens over raw colors.

Philosophy SSOT: [`DESIGN.md`](../../DESIGN.md) **Interaction philosophy** (why). This file (how + checklists). Design Skills supplement visual judgment only — they do not duplicate or override project interaction rules here.

### Design Skill invocation contract

Read the relevant `DESIGN.md` chapters first (especially `Interaction philosophy`, motion, tokens, information density, and UI/product behavior); do not load the full Design Skill collection by default. Design Skills are optional methods for visual judgment, not project authority. For visual and interaction decisions, use this fixed priority: user’s explicit task requirements → product docs, ADRs, and locked task behavior → `DESIGN.md` → this rule → the selected Design Skill → shadcn or other component defaults.

#### Default design baseline

Only for creating, refactoring, or reviewing UI, consider these on demand; they remain subordinate to `DESIGN.md`:

- `design-taste-frontend` — landing, portfolio, and anti-generic frontend direction.
- `redesign-existing-projects` — audit-led visual upgrades to an existing interface without breaking functionality.

#### Specialist capabilities

Load a specialist only when the task explicitly matches it. By default, choose at most one specialist per task unless the user explicitly asks to compare multiple approaches:

- Brand identity and visual world: `brandkit`.
- Strong motion or GSAP: `gpt-taste`.
- High-end visual review: `high-end-visual-design`.
- Image reference to frontend: `image-to-code`.
- Web visual reference images: `imagegen-frontend-web`.
- Mobile visual reference images: `imagegen-frontend-mobile`.
- Industrial or brutalist style: `industrial-brutalist-ui`.
- Minimal editorial style: `minimalist-ui`.
- Stitch workflow: `stitch-design-taste`.

Even when a specialist matches, do not directly adopt its hardcoded colors, fonts, radii, shadows, spacing, animation, or page structure. Map useful suggestions to `DESIGN.md` tokens and interaction boundaries first. In particular, `gpt-taste` scrolling pins, strong motion, and narrative pacing are allowed only when compatible with Gloaming’s nearly invisible motion and reading-first principles. `image-to-code` and `imagegen-*` outputs are reference material, not a new design system or product requirement. Industrial and minimalist styles are explicit choices; never apply them automatically to Reader, Admin, or ordinary product pages. Do not add an unauthorized dependency, generated image, motion library, or product feature because a Design Skill recommends it.

Do not load a Design Skill for ordinary bug fixes, copy-only adjustments, or pure logic changes. The role of a UI Design Skill is to supplement project design judgment, never to replace `DESIGN.md`, product rules, or this behavior boundary.

### UI design judgment (before styling)

**UI rule stack:** apply the Design Skill invocation contract above: user task → product/ADR/locked behavior → [`DESIGN.md`](../../DESIGN.md) Interaction philosophy → this section → the selected Design Skill (**visual only**) → shadcn / component defaults **last**. Library form patterns do not override project interaction judgment.

**Read order:** `DESIGN.md` Interaction philosophy → this section → UI implementation ladder below → the selected Design Skill if visual polish is in scope.

**Default priority:** Remove → Simplify → Combine → Clarify → Polish. Never scaffold Label + Description + Card + Button first and style later.

**Decision flow (every new or changed UI surface):**

1. Product task — what must complete here?
2. Minimum information — what cannot be inferred from title, tab, grouping, or control?
3. Minimum interactions — fewest controls that finish the task
4. Context inference — what does the user already know?
5. Merge — can related actions share one control context?
6. Delete — run Anti-Redundancy Checklist
7. Polish — project tokens + shadcn + the selected Design Skill

#### Information economy

Each visible element must provide **unique** information or **unique** action. Before adding Label, Description, Helper text, Badge, status text, Heading, Divider, Card, Button, Icon button, or secondary action, ask:

- Why does this exist?
- Is this already represented elsewhere on the same surface?
- If I remove it, does comprehension, discoverability, or function clearly suffer?

If not → remove. **Not** “labels/descriptions/cards/buttons are bad” — keep any element with unique information, action, context, or discoverability for that audience and task.

#### Behavior boundary (do not infer product behavior)

UI judgment may merge controls, remove copy, or relocate actions. It must **not** change persistence, fetch timing, confirmation, or side effects without product/task basis.

**Preserve unless the task explicitly requires otherwise:** explicit Save/Submit, APIs that save per field or per row, manual refresh, confirm dialogs, fetch-on-open, debounced auto-save, optimistic updates, delete confirmations.

**Do not introduce without product/task basis:** auto-save, blur-save, immediate or optimistic persistence, automatic fetch or refresh on mount, automatic submission, automatic deletion, implicit confirmation, hidden side effects.

If simplification would replace Save with auto-save (or similar) → mark **PRODUCT / BEHAVIOR**, keep current behavior, stop (`core` decision gate). Execution detail: [`DESIGN.md`](../../DESIGN.md) Interaction philosophy → **UI vs product behavior**.

#### Interaction compression

Assign every action to its **object** and **task** first:

| Pattern | Prefer |
| --- | --- |
| Load list + pick item | One Select/Combobox with contextual refresh (icon in trigger row), not Fetch button + Select |
| Toggle a setting | Switch with one label naming the **setting**, not label + "启用/Enabled" status text |
| Edit one record | One save **surface** per editing context when product already uses form-level save — do not remove Save or switch to auto-save without product decision |
| Row maintenance | Icon actions on the row (edit/delete/test), not a separate action bar for the same row |

Standalone buttons stay when the action is page-scoped, destructive, or needs primary emphasis.

#### Contextual actions

Place actions adjacent to what they modify — field row end, Select trigger group, table row — instead of a detached button that repeats the same task.

#### State representation

- **Switch:** control = state. Label names the setting (`AI 模型`), not on/off. No parallel "启用" / "Enabled" text.
- **Select / Combobox:** selected value = state. No redundant "已选择" badge.
- **Badge / status line:** only for health, errors, or saved-vs-draft — not duplicate control state.
- **Form vs collection:** no redundant status beside a form Switch; table/list status columns for scanning many rows are OK.
- **a11y:** `aria-label` or visually hidden name when the visible UI is icon-only — not a second visible status word.

#### Semantic redundancy

Do not stack the same fact in title + description + field label + helper + badge. Page title + section + field name often already answer "what is this?"

Description/helper text: **only** for non-obvious constraints (format, side effects, irreversible ops) — not restating the field name in prose.

#### Admin UI (`features/admin/**`, `/admin/**`)

**Scope:** stricter economy for admin/configuration only — not a global mandate to strip labels, descriptions, or text buttons from reader/consumer UI.

Operators understand domain terms. Apply stricter economy:

- One-line page intro when the task is non-obvious; skip when nav + layout already state the job.
- No consumer-style helper on every field; Region/API Key/Model need labels, not paragraphs.
- Prefer flat sections and row actions over Card → Card → Heading stacks for one task.
- Tables/lists: inline icon actions; status column only when not inferable from row opacity/disabled state.
- Same `DESIGN.md` tokens; denser spacing OK — not a separate theme.

#### Anti-Redundancy Checklist (post-design, before polish)

**Element audit** — for each visible element:

- What unique information or action does it provide?
- Already represented elsewhere?
- Can this action merge into another control?
- Removable without harm?

**Interaction audit** — for each user task:

- How many steps and independent controls?
- Any controls separated without a task reason?
- Can a standalone button become inline/contextual?

**Density audit** — flag and remove:

- redundant labels, descriptions, helper text, status text
- unnecessary buttons, cards, dividers, headings
- duplicated actions; decorative chrome without function

Do **not** treat the checklist as “delete all labels/descriptions/badges/cards/buttons” or “icons always win.” Re-check against **Behavior boundary** before removing Save, confirm, or fetch controls.

#### Component patterns (Gloaming)

| Control | Rule |
| --- | --- |
| `Switch` | One label = setting name. Horizontal `Field` OK. No "启用" beside switch. |
| `Select` / `Combobox` | Label = object (`模型`, `默认模型`). Refresh/fetch as sibling icon in trigger row when lists are remote. |
| `Field` + `FieldDescription` | Max one description per field; must add constraint not in label. No Description + helper saying the same thing. |
| `Card` | One task or one grouping level. No card inside card for a single form. Prefer bordered section when elevation adds nothing. |
| Page header | `h1` + optional one-line subtitle. No subtitle that repeats tab label. |
| Save | Form-level or explicit dirty-state Save when product uses batch save; per-row/per-key Save when API requires it — **never** swap Save for auto-save without **PRODUCT / BEHAVIOR** approval |

### UI implementation ladder (visual polish last)

Product UI must look like Gloaming (`DESIGN.md`) **after** interaction judgment above passes. Atoms are a means, not the goal.

1. Prefer **shadcn** atoms in `components/ui/` (add via CLI: `pnpm exec shadcn add …` from `apps/web`). Use variants/props first.
2. Polish with **Tailwind `className`** on those atoms when defaults fall short.
3. Compose atoms + light structural markup if still short.
4. **Last resort:** native DOM + Tailwind when no suitable atom exists.

Do not hand-roll a parallel control system. Do not ship “used shadcn but ugly/default tooling” UIs.

**System UI language:** Chinese for labels, nav, empty states, toasts, placeholders. Content field *values* may be EN/ZH.

**Base UI gotchas:** `Button` + `Link` → `nativeButton={false}`. Tabs active → `data-active`. Toggle pressed → `data-pressed`. Segmented filters: prefer `Tabs`; override list `h-8` with `h-auto` and pad triggers — avoid fixed-height fights.

## Auth

Soft UX only: cookie presence in `proxy.ts` (`better-auth.session_token` / `__Secure-…`), session + **401 → sign-in** in the client.
**Real auth** is Better Auth on `apps/backend` (`auth.api.getSession` / `requireAuth`) — not the Next soft gate.
`/admin/**` must check session `user.role` with `@gloaming/shared/auth/policy` before rendering admin content; hiding nav links is UX only, not authorization.
Any backend-backed admin data must also be protected by Hono `requireAdmin`; never rely on `proxy.ts` or client checks as the security boundary.
`DELETE /api/auth/logout` is a Next handler so HttpOnly BA session cookie(s) clear on this origin, then Hono `sign-out`.
Password/username bounds from `@gloaming/shared/auth/policy` — do not re-declare in web Zod.

## Prototype / stub UI

Admin/content screens backed by static arrays, mock data, or UI-only toasts must be explicitly labeled as prototype/stub in both source comments and user-facing Chinese copy. Do not imply persistence, publishing, CMS sync, or backend integration until the Hono content module exists.
